    "field": "Climate change adaptation",
    "problem": "Existing assessments of climate change adaptation options are inadequate as they focus on slow, uniform ecosystem changes, failing to prepare for the sudden, large-scale, and patchy ecosystem crashes that climate change can trigger.",
    "method": "To build stakeholder resilience to ecosystem crashes, the paper proposes a framework that assesses adaptive options based on the portability of the ecosystem service and the location flexibility of the stakeholder.",
    "task": "The task is to develop a conceptual framework for identifying adaptation options to sudden ecosystem crashes by assessing the portability of the service and the locational flexibility of the stakeholder.",
